    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d34">

                <pb facs="0192" n="26" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg26"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 832.461/2</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Morgan to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-07-05T11:00:00-03:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 5, 1917, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A remarkable demonstration of friendship for the United States and a further step
                    toward cooperation with the cause of the Allies marked the commemoration
                    yesterday of Independence Day by the Brazilian Government. The President of the
                    Republic visited the flagship of Admiral Caperton’s squadron and on the
                    initiative of the Minister of Marine there was a street parade of marines and
                    bluejackets in which the crews of the American, French and British war vessels
                    in Rio de Janeiro Harbor participated in the company of a Brazilian naval
                    contingent, a total of 2,600 men. Our boys received a popular ovation which was
                    as sincere as it was spontaneous.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
